# DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) Principle

## Core Rules
- Extract repeated logic into shared utilities/services
- Limit similar patterns to 2 instances before refactoring
- Reuse over rewrite - check existing utilities first

## Implementation Guidelines
- Use shared hooks in [src/hooks](mdc:src/hooks) for common React patterns
- Utilize shared services in [src/services](mdc:src/services) for business logic
- Leverage common utilities in [src/lib](mdc:src/lib) for helper functions

## Common Locations for Reuse
- Configuration: [src/lib/config.ts](mdc:src/lib/config.ts)
- API Integration: [src/integrations](mdc:src/integrations)
- Shared Components: [src/components](mdc:src/components)

## Validation
Before creating new functionality:
1. Search existing utilities
2. Check for similar patterns
3. Consider extracting if pattern appears more than twice

